<!-- What is Currents Section -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="card" style="padding: 2rem;">
      <h2>What is Currents News API?</h2>
      <p>
        Currents is a REST news API that delivers real-time and historical articles from a source directory spanning 168 countries and 20+ languages. Responses are clean JSON with metadata, descriptions, source URLs, available content fields, and filters for country, language, category, date range, and search keywords.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- How the News API Works Section -->
<section class="section section-light integration-examples" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="text-center mb-5">
      <h2>How the News API Works</h2>
      <p>Send one HTTP request with your API key. The API returns a JSON list of articles.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div class="card" style="padding: 2rem;">
        <h3>1. Send a request</h3>
        <pre style="font-size: 0.875rem; overflow-x: auto; background: var(--bg-lighter); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem;"><code>curl -G https://api.currentsapi.services/v1/latest-news \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -d language=en -d page_size=3</code></pre>
        <ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
          <li><code>/v1/latest-news</code> returns the newest indexed articles. Filter them by <code>language</code>, <code>country</code>, and <code>category</code>.</li>
          <li><code>/v1/search</code> finds articles by <code>keywords</code> in a date window set by <code>start_date</code> and <code>end_date</code>.</li>
          <li>A free key allows 250 requests per UTC day and up to 20 articles per request. Free searches have a 30-day lookback and a 7-day max date span per request.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 0;"><a href="/en/register">Get a free API key</a> · <a href="/en/docs/latest_news">Latest news reference</a> · <a href="/en/docs/search">Search reference</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="card" style="padding: 2rem;">
        <h3>2. Read the JSON response</h3>
        <pre style="font-size: 0.875rem; overflow-x: auto; background: var(--bg-lighter); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem;"><code>{
  "status": "ok",
  "news": [
    {
      "id": "f8f18e4b-c66e-47ca-9f7d-54f03e431a77",
      "title": "Chipmaker expands data-center investment",
      "description": "The company announced a new multi-year expansion plan...",
      "url": "https://example.com/business/chipmaker-expands",
      "author": "Editorial Desk",
      "image": "https://example.com/images/chipmaker.jpg",
      "language": "en",
      "category": ["science_technology", "economy_business_finance"],
      "published": "2026-03-24 11:10:00 +0000"
    }
  ],
  "page": 1
}</code></pre>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">Each article has an ID, title, description, link to the original story, language, categories, and publication time. <code>author</code> and <code>image</code> are <code>null</code> when the publisher does not provide them. The values above are examples.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

